00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:07.269 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello i'm christopher and we're at my  restaurant here at mihikeli tacoma  company and today i'm going to show you  how to make our kachita zepoyo aka slap  in the face grilled chicken and a  toasted tortilla melted cheese but today  we're gonna do with a twist of special  recipe that we do with my friend matt  kim and i so matt kim is one of my best  friends that we met a long time ago in  an empty parking lot when i started  selling tacos on the street he shows up  in his car i did not have a clue who  this kid is pops up his trunk pulls out  a cooler and all of a sudden he's like  the most popular kid on the block this  uni starts coming out i never seen uni  in my life and that's when i was  introduced to uni for the very first  time so we decided to put on everything  on the menu we put it on tacos and  quesadillas but my favorite by far was  the uni on top of our famous cachetta i  call it slap in the face because it's  spicy it's crunchy it is in your face  and it's amazing so to start off with  our cachetta  we are going to start off with our  all-natural corn tortillas we are going  to dehydrate those we're going to put  them on a plancha we're going to sit in  there for about five to 10 minutes we're  going to go on to our foyo asado and  we're going to start off with our  marinade first we have california chile  powder guajillo powdered onion powder  garlic powder cumin pepper salt and  sugar so now we're gonna go on with our  acidity so we're gonna do two portions  for something like this you need about  two oranges we need about one lime and  we're gonna give it a nice mix so the  acidity is very important because it  helps break down all the ingredients and  it also combines them together once it's  nice and smooth dunk in our chicken and  we're gonna give it a nice rub for  polyasolo in the restaurant we love to  use chicken thighs and chicken leg we  find that it's the juiciest part of the  chicken and it's the most flavorful of  all so we're gonna give it a nice mix a  minute or so make sure it's nice and  fully coated then we put it in the  fridge and let it rest there so while  that's resting and doing its magic we're  going to jump on to our pickled onions  time management is so important in the  kitchen so we're going to multitask a  little bit so we're going to take one  red onion cut it in half and give it  some nice fine julienne then we're going  to add our dried oregano make sure you  crush it very finely so what i like to  do with my oregano i like to grab a good  bunch and put it between my hands and  rub it very firmly so it turns into  powder and that's the best way for  oregano to do what it's supposed to do  we're gonna add a good amount of vinegar  you could use white vinegar red wine  vinegar apple cider vinegar whatever you  have at home season it with salt and  that's to give it a nice mix a nice rub  and again it goes into the fridge and  let it do its magic so food in my family  means everything it's the time that we  all get together forget it for mad at  each other celebrate things and it's all  good moments good happy memories it's a  way to remember our ancestors our  grandmas special recipes that are true  to our family mexicali it is actually  the place where i was raised and grew up  down in mexicali baja california i  learned a lot about hard work and  dedication i moved to la and i decided  that when i opened my first restaurant  or taco stand i was going to name it  after my hometown of mexicali baja  california and a lot of the influence  was this cuisine we showcased here at  the restaurant and i think it's proper  that we name it  one of the most important parts of our  cachita is actually our signature sauce  that goes inside chipotle aioli sauce it  sounds fancy but it's really just  mayonnaise with chipotle and a little  bit of seasoning we're gonna get our  mayonnaise we're gonna add a good amount  of chipotle sauce if you like it spicy  with a cake the way i do i would add  extra chipotle peppers in there we're  gonna add a little bit of salt sweeping  it out and we're gonna add a good amount  of lime juice give it a nice whisk so  it's nice and smooth and if you're like  me there's never enough heat put some  more of that chipotle on your ioli and  then again put it aside so our chicken's  been marinating about 15 to 20 minutes  we're gonna grab our chicken put it on  the grill you wanna go medium on this  one if you go too high you're gonna burn  the outside and the inside is not gonna  cook now it's very important when you're  grilling your chicken you gotta flip it  multiple times back and forth look for  those beautiful grill marks you know for  the smoke signals for the fire bursting  everywhere on the grill it's not like a  steak steaky let it sit there high heat  flip it once maybe and then it's ready  to go chicken you have to really  dedicate some time and give it some care  and you just want to get that nice char  oh that looks so good so now the chicken  is grilling matt is going to do his  thing he's so excited this is what he  lives for so he's going to crack it open  he's got this really cool device that he  uses and he's going to scoop out the  golden uni so he takes the uni he sits  it in water to rinse it off a little bit  and then it's ready to go what's so cool  about matt is that he's just as suspense  race as i am this guy will go rock  climbing scuba diving spear fishing all  the things that i love to do but i don't  really have the guts to so i kind of put  him to the test first he gets it done  then i say okay it's doable let's jump  on it we have an amazing relationship we  know each other very very well  especially when it comes to food so  we're always eating out and hanging out  and reminiscing and doing new adventures  all the time so now everything's coming  together we are getting very close to  the end we're gonna grab our chicken  take it off the heat and we're gonna let  it rest just as you would escape set it  aside for five to ten minutes while  that's doing its thing we're gonna grab  our tostadas nice and dehydrated crispy  but we're not done yet we're gonna load  it up with monterey jack cheese we're  gonna put them on the grill and we're  looking for those beautiful gooey cheesy  bubbly signs of cheese heaven our cheese  is doing its magical gooeyness we're  gonna go onto our chicken it's been  rested we're gonna slice it into cubes i  would say half an inch both ways i like  to cut it in perfect cubes it's for  presentation it's for a really good bite  so now it's time to put this all  together so we're going to load our  tostada with chicken so each bite is as  perfect as the first so now we're going  to go on and dress our cachetta with our  delicious aioli sauce and now it's time  to customize it this is where the  mexicali style comes in we're known for  customization every pallet is different  so finally now it's time to enjoy this  with my friend matt what are you gonna  put on it  the usual everything i personally like  to have some chili herbal it's spicy  it's smoky i like to put some aguacate  some avocado sauce and i like to put a  little bit of cabbage for a bite for a  nice texture and then we're going to add  some pickled red onions these are my  absolute favorite i put them on  everything and then this is where matt  kim comes in and he's going to show off  his skills with our golden uni and if  you're going to go with uni might as  well go all out you got to make it rain  and matt does that very very well so  we're going to load it up with uni just  how we like it brings back so much  memories this is the start of our  friendship salute cheers  each bite is like ocean meets mexicali  streets each memories fun times with  matt and i ah it is my favorite thing to  eat the uni the ocean i mean it's your  story with my story put together on a  bike dude this is perfect this is us man  right here so we are all done i hope you  guys love the cachitas as much as i do  try it at home it really is a slap in  the face  oh yes  nice there you go  [Music]

